IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
-- AFTER, the window's opening edge: the examples from AFTER.md, with a trace
-- each so the instants the window produces are visible.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Buyer, Seller
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER
                         deliver
                         order

-- The cooling-off window. The seller delivers at 10; the buyer may order
-- again after a three-day cooling-off period, within 30 days of that:
-- the window is [13, 43].
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`cooling off` MEANS
  PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN 30
  HENCE (PARTY Buyer MUST order AFTER 3 WITHIN 30)
  LEST  BREACH

-- 12 is before the window opens: not performance, and the run says so
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver AT 10
  PARTY Buyer DOES order AT 12

-- 41 is in time: the window closes at 43, not at 40
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver AT 10
  PARTY Buyer DOES order AT 41

-- 44 is late
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver AT 10
  PARTY Buyer DOES order AT 44

-- The statutory two-offset window, "not less than 3 nor more than 30 days
-- after delivery": both edges from the delivery, [13, 40]. 41 is late.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`two offsets` MEANS
  PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN 30
  HENCE (PARTY Buyer MUST order AFTER 3 WITHIN 30 OF THE JOIN)
  LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `two offsets` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver AT 10
  PARTY Buyer DOES order AT 41

-- A right that vests and never expires: from 13 on, whenever.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
vested MEANS
  PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN 30
  HENCE (PARTY Buyer MAY order AFTER 3)
  LEST  BREACH

#TRACE vested AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Seller DOES deliver AT 10
  PARTY Buyer DOES order AT 1000

-- The absolute forms, on a trace whose clock is date serials: opens three
-- days after 1 June, closes on 30 June.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`by june` MEANS
  PARTY Buyer MUST pay 100 AFTER 3 BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 30)

#TRACE `by june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay 100 AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 4))

#TRACE `by june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay 100 AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 1))
